  "version": 1,
  "about": "Rush Taxi city (stage 3), modelled loosely on Kaohsiung: the Love River across the middle, the harbour and the sea on the west, the old Hamasen/Yancheng streets north-west, Zuoying/Fengshan parks north-east, downtown south-east. Public places use their real names; shops and commercial buildings get our own names. Hand-made layout: a road grid every 60 m (lines at ±30, ±90 … ±330), blocks 46 m square centred on multiples of 60, a river across the middle (z −18…18) with four bridges and two jump ramps, four districts (one per quarter), parks and 32 landmarks. Buildings inside ordinary blocks are generated from each district's style. Landmark shapes are listed as primitives in block-local metres (y = height of the centre): [\"box\", x, y, z, sx, sy, sz, colour], [\"cyl\", x, y, z, r, h, colour], [\"cone\", x, y, z, r, h, colour] (negative h points down), [\"sph\", x, y, z, r, colour], [\"tor\", x, y, z, R, tube, colour, yaw]. Doors name the road the entrance is on: n = +z, s = −z, e = +x, w = −x.",
